The **Lovelace** theme is a brutalist, nearly no-CSS archive theme that embraces browser defaults for maximum speed and simplicity. It renders in monospace with minimal styling, and is named after [Ada Lovelace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ada_Lovelace).

- [Live preview](https://demo.buttondown.com/long-way-round/archive/)
- [Source CSS](https://github.com/buttondown/themes/blob/main/themes/lovelace/assets/styles.css)

You can switch to the Lovelace theme—and tweak any of the settings below—from your [archive settings](https://buttondown.com/settings/archives).

